3.3 System Modules

1. User Input Module

Collects the story prompt, character name, setting, tone, and art style from the user through the homepage.

2. Story Outline Module

Uses Gemini Flash to create a structured five-panel comic outline with panel titles, scene descriptions, and image prompts.

3. Story Generation Module

Uses Gemini Pro to generate detailed narration and dialogues based on the outline.

4. Image Generation Module

Uses Stable Diffusion through Hugging Face Diffusers to generate illustrations for individual panels.

5. Layout Builder Module

Combines the generated images and story content into a structured panel layout.

6. PDF Export Module

Uses FPDF to organize the comic panels, images, and text into a downloadable PDF.

7. Web Interface Module

Uses HTML, CSS, and Jinja2 to display the input form, comic preview, and export success page.

3.4 Data Flow
3.5 User Interface Design

The application contains three primary web pages:

index.html: Collects user input using a structured form.

comic_preview.html: Displays each generated panel with its image, title, scene description, captions, and narration.

export_success.html: Displays confirmation after the comic export process.

The interface should use clear labels, readable typography, responsive styling, and simple navigation.

